    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Question\n\n`MiniPick.builtin.resume()` will throw error if called before any picker was called first.\r\nIs there a way to check if there are pickers before resuming, or make it fail silently if there are no pickers?",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.pick</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">MiniPick.builtin.resume()</code> will throw error if called before any picker was called first.<br>\nIs there a way to check if there are pickers before resuming, or make it fail silently if there are no pickers?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.pick\nQuestion\nMiniPick.builtin.resume() will throw error if called before any picker was called first.\nIs there a way to check if there are pickers before resuming, or make it fail silently if there are no pickers?",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
        "id": "DIC_kwDOFoksYM4CAgqN",
        "isAnswerable": true,
        "name": "Q&A",
        "slug": "q-a",
        "updatedAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z"
    },
    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2026-04-06T09:00:03Z",
    "comment_count": 2,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58370433?u=f27c5d8743e4a42fc8bc9fe3bd6484f6571061cb&v=4",
                "login": "abeldekat",
                "resourcePath": "/abeldekat",
                "url": "https://github.com/abeldekat"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I don't see a direct way, as [H.pickers.latest](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/402ee6c6ec8ea44b22330446c8fb4e615fd3953e/lua/mini/pick.lua#L1573) is private.\r\n\r\nPerhaps something like this?\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.g.mapleader = \" \"\r\n\r\nrequire(\"mini.pick\").setup()\r\n\r\nlocal can_resume = false\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"User\", {\r\n  pattern = \"MiniPickStart\",\r\n  once = true,\r\n  callback = function() can_resume = true end,\r\n})\r\n\r\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<Leader>fr\", function()\r\n  if not can_resume then return end\r\n  MiniPick.builtin.resume()\r\nend, { desc = \"Resume\" })\r\n\r\n```",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I don't see a direct way, as <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/402ee6c6ec8ea44b22330446c8fb4e615fd3953e/lua/mini/pick.lua#L1573\">H.pickers.latest</a> is private.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Perhaps something like this?</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.g.mapleader = &quot; &quot;\n\nrequire(&quot;mini.pick&quot;).setup()\n\nlocal can_resume = false\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(&quot;User&quot;, {\n  pattern = &quot;MiniPickStart&quot;,\n  once = true,\n  callback = function() can_resume = true end,\n})\n\nvim.keymap.set(&quot;n&quot;, &quot;&lt;Leader&gt;fr&quot;, function()\n  if not can_resume then return end\n  MiniPick.builtin.resume()\nend, { desc = &quot;Resume&quot; })\n\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">g</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">mapleader</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span> <span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>mini.pick<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>()\n\n<span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">can_resume</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">false</span>\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_create_autocmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>User<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, {\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">pattern</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>MiniPickStart<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>,\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">once</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">true</span>,\n  <span class=\"pl-en\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>() <span class=\"pl-smi\">can_resume</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">true</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n})\n\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">set</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>&lt;Leader&gt;fr<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">not</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">can_resume</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">then</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniPick</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">builtin</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">resume</span>()\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">desc</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>Resume<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>})\n</pre></div>",
            "bodyText": "I don't see a direct way, as H.pickers.latest is private.\nPerhaps something like this?\nvim.g.mapleader = \" \"\n\nrequire(\"mini.pick\").setup()\n\nlocal can_resume = false\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"User\", {\n  pattern = \"MiniPickStart\",\n  once = true,\n  callback = function() can_resume = true end,\n})\n\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<Leader>fr\", function()\n  if not can_resume then return end\n  MiniPick.builtin.resume()\nend, { desc = \"Resume\" })",
