                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "@echasnovski It is not a problem, I agree with it throwing an error. What was bothering me was how jarring neovim messages can be with stack traces (it's great for debugging, jarring when you're working and get such an error when erroneously trying to resume pickers that don't exist yet).\r\n\r\n`pcall` works, I've thought of that. I think I'll show a shorter and nicer message with `vim.notify` if the call throws an error, but wanted to ask here before I decided what to do, in case there was a better approach.\r\n\r\nThanks for the quick response, `mini.vim` really takes `neovim` to a new level.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/echasnovski/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski\">@echasnovski</a> It is not a problem, I agree with it throwing an error. What was bothering me was how jarring neovim messages can be with stack traces (it's great for debugging, jarring when you're working and get such an error when erroneously trying to resume pickers that don't exist yet).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">pcall</code> works, I've thought of that. I think I'll show a shorter and nicer message with <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.notify</code> if the call throws an error, but wanted to ask here before I decided what to do, in case there was a better approach.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks for the quick response, <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.vim</code> really takes <code class=\"notranslate\">neovim</code> to a new level.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "@echasnovski It is not a problem, I agree with it throwing an error. What was bothering me was how jarring neovim messages can be with stack traces (it's great for debugging, jarring when you're working and get such an error when erroneously trying to resume pickers that don't exist yet).\npcall works, I've thought of that. I think I'll show a shorter and nicer message with vim.notify if the call throws an error, but wanted to ask here before I decided what to do, in case there was a better approach.\nThanks for the quick response, mini.vim really takes neovim to a new level.",
